1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:00,960
(All characters, locations,
and events are fictional

2
00:00:00,985 --> 00:00:01,912
and for entertainment
purposes only.

3
00:00:01,936 --> 00:00:02,952
No actions depicted are intended
to be encouraged or endorsed.

4
00:00:02,984 --> 00:00:04,292
Animals were specially trained
and supervised by professionals.

5
00:00:04,317 --> 00:00:05,491
Viewer discretion is advised.)

6
00:00:06,590 --> 00:00:09,475
A lot of people think golf
is a game of perfection,

7
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:11,164
a game of precision.

8
00:00:11,189 --> 00:00:13,828
But the longer you play,
the more you realize

9
00:00:13,853 --> 00:00:15,408
the hardest thing to control

10
00:00:15,433 --> 00:00:17,346
isn't your distance
or your swing.

11
00:00:17,370 --> 00:00:19,788
It's yourself.
And your own heart.

12
00:00:21,016 --> 00:00:23,130
Some days, nothing goes
the way you hoped,

13
00:00:23,155 --> 00:00:24,603
and you barely
want to keep playing.

14
00:00:24,628 --> 00:00:28,128
But on a good day, you never
want the 18th hole to end.

15
00:00:28,589 --> 00:00:30,394
No matter what kind of day
you're having,

16
00:00:30,419 --> 00:00:32,577
the hardest thing
to control in golf

17
00:00:32,601 --> 00:00:34,661
isn't your swing or your score.

18
00:00:35,955 --> 00:00:37,831
It's yourself.
And your own heart.

19
00:00:39,002 --> 00:00:41,262
Focus on the next shot,

20
00:00:41,651 --> 00:00:43,580
not the score
waiting at the 18th.

21
00:00:46,884 --> 00:00:50,681
(Pro Khaoklong:
Keerattriya Foocharoen)

22
00:00:58,554 --> 00:01:02,031
♪ Everyone can tell
by the way you stare ♪

23
00:01:02,654 --> 00:01:04,408
♪ Sneaking little looks
when I'm unaware ♪

24
00:01:04,433 --> 00:01:08,532
♪ It's plain to see ♪

25
00:01:08,557 --> 00:01:10,257
♪ I know exactly
what you think of me ♪

26
00:01:10,282 --> 00:01:13,655
♪ First to watch my stories
every time ♪

27
00:01:14,309 --> 00:01:16,007
♪ You remember
every fave of mine ♪

28
00:01:16,032 --> 00:01:19,724
♪ Everywhere I go,
you're by my side ♪

29
00:01:19,749 --> 00:01:21,792
♪ Don't tell me
there's nothing on your mind ♪

30
00:01:21,817 --> 00:01:24,715
♪ So when are you
gonna say the words? ♪

31
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:26,630
♪ Don't keep me waiting
till it hurts ♪

32
00:01:26,655 --> 00:01:29,482
♪ The way you act,
I know you're into me ♪

33
00:01:29,507 --> 00:01:32,364
♪ That racing heart
gives you away so easily ♪

34
00:01:32,389 --> 00:01:36,234
♪ But I'll play clueless,
just wait and see ♪

35
00:01:36,259 --> 00:01:38,259
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

36
00:01:38,284 --> 00:01:41,081
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

37
00:01:41,106 --> 00:01:44,497
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

38
00:01:44,522 --> 00:01:49,279
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

39
00:01:49,304 --> 00:01:51,304
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

40
00:01:52,634 --> 00:01:54,244
The reason I called you home

41
00:01:54,269 --> 00:01:56,054
is because I don't want
the golf course

42
00:01:56,079 --> 00:01:57,846
falling into
someone else's hands.

43
00:01:57,886 --> 00:01:59,019
What do you mean?

44
00:01:59,044 --> 00:02:00,864
The course is about
to go under, Nana.

45
00:02:00,889 --> 00:02:02,777
Why does it have to be me?

46
00:02:04,194 --> 00:02:06,344
I assigned Belle
to be your assistant.

47
00:02:06,369 --> 00:02:08,179
Whatever you need, Miss Nana,

48
00:02:08,204 --> 00:02:10,363
I'll make it happen.
You can count on me.

49
00:02:10,388 --> 00:02:11,720
I want to learn how to play golf.

50
00:02:11,745 --> 00:02:15,216
This is Pro Venus.
She'll be teaching you golf.

51
00:02:16,402 --> 00:02:19,259
I'll teach you
if you can meet one condition.

52
00:02:19,284 --> 00:02:21,284
- Here's your sandwich.
- Thanks.

53
00:02:32,964 --> 00:02:36,333
Mmm! Everything from your cafe
is so good.

54
00:02:36,535 --> 00:02:38,678
Aren't you eating
a little too much, Nana?

55
00:02:38,967 --> 00:02:40,523
But it's really good!

56
00:02:41,339 --> 00:02:43,132
Besides, I've been
working out a lot.

57
00:02:43,157 --> 00:02:44,618
I practice golf every day.

58
00:02:44,847 --> 00:02:47,130
So how are things
at the golf course lately?

59
00:02:47,284 --> 00:02:50,944
I haven't really done much yet.
I'm still gathering information.

60
00:02:50,969 --> 00:02:53,403
You're there
to check out the course.

61
00:02:53,428 --> 00:02:57,426
Not check out
the gorgeous golf pro.

62
00:02:58,496 --> 00:03:00,089
- What's that supposed to mean?
- Oh?

63
00:03:00,114 --> 00:03:02,701
What is going on?
Spill it, Nana.

64
00:03:03,655 --> 00:03:05,696
A girl needs a little motivation

65
00:03:05,721 --> 00:03:07,989
to get up early
for golf every day.

66
00:03:08,728 --> 00:03:12,075
Ohhh. So you're trying
to turn pro the fast way?

67
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:14,100
Oh, shut up, Pim.

68
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:15,635
How'd you know?

69
00:03:16,810 --> 00:03:20,124
You know what?
We need to pick a day

70
00:03:20,149 --> 00:03:22,149
and go visit Nana
at the golf course.

71
00:03:22,912 --> 00:03:25,508
Come by. Maybe one of you

72
00:03:25,533 --> 00:03:27,778
will have an idea
to get this place booming again.

73
00:03:28,827 --> 00:03:31,620
I'm dying to go back.

74
00:03:31,645 --> 00:03:35,829
I miss my easy life and
shopping on the Champs-Élysées.

75
00:03:35,854 --> 00:03:38,863
Oh, my brother said
he ran into Nana over there.

76
00:03:38,969 --> 00:03:41,303
- Ohh... dreamy Nut?
- Yeah.

77
00:03:41,328 --> 00:03:43,454
Yeah. It was totally by chance.

78
00:03:43,479 --> 00:03:45,752
I think Nut was there
on a business trip.

79
00:03:45,777 --> 00:03:47,569
But right now, anyone who's good

80
00:03:47,594 --> 00:03:49,483
with finance, accounting,
or marketing,

81
00:03:49,507 --> 00:03:52,567
please come save me.
I'm buried in numbers all day.

82
00:03:52,599 --> 00:03:54,344
My brain is fried.

83
00:03:54,854 --> 00:03:57,660
Don't stress yet. Eat first.

84
00:03:57,834 --> 00:04:01,224
- Keep eating. Have some more.
- Try this. No stressing.

85
00:04:01,249 --> 00:04:04,849
- I want to meet Nut too.
- He's so handsome.

86
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,910
I brought you something yummy.

87
00:04:14,286 --> 00:04:17,757
Ooh, that looks good.
Where did you get it?

88
00:04:18,108 --> 00:04:21,777
From my friend's cafe.
Try it. It's really good.

89
00:04:23,986 --> 00:04:26,877
I scheduled the Set A caddies
for you this afternoon.

90
00:04:26,902 --> 00:04:28,221
They're all really excited.

91
00:04:29,046 --> 00:04:31,855
That thing I asked you
to look into...

92
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:32,942
I was right, wasn't I?

93
00:04:38,950 --> 00:04:40,042
I knew it.

94
00:04:43,889 --> 00:04:45,239
What do you want to do next?

95
00:04:48,875 --> 00:04:50,138
Easy.

96
00:04:59,850 --> 00:05:01,769
I'm redesigning
the caddie uniforms

97
00:05:01,794 --> 00:05:05,496
because you spend more time with
our customers than anyone else.

98
00:05:05,830 --> 00:05:10,129
That makes every one of you
an ambassador for this course.

99
00:05:10,708 --> 00:05:14,977
If the course is the heart,
then the caddies are its pulse.

100
00:05:15,002 --> 00:05:17,357
We don't dress well just so
other people will look at us.

101
00:05:17,382 --> 00:05:19,688
We dress well
to feel confident in ourselves.

102
00:05:20,003 --> 00:05:22,970
I believe that
when you feel good about yourself

103
00:05:22,995 --> 00:05:24,851
and feel happy
in what you're wearing,

104
00:05:24,876 --> 00:05:28,327
you pass that positive energy
on to our guests.

105
00:05:30,501 --> 00:05:31,502
Belle, sweetie.

106
00:05:32,010 --> 00:05:34,399
Once we finalize
the new uniform design,

107
00:05:34,424 --> 00:05:36,124
how long will production take?

108
00:05:36,149 --> 00:05:38,499
Not long.
I've already spoken to the shop.

109
00:05:38,524 --> 00:05:40,721
- I asked them to rush it.
- Perfect.

110
00:05:42,750 --> 00:05:44,035
Thank you so much, everyone.

111
00:05:53,343 --> 00:05:57,716
Wow, so you're changing
the caddie uniforms, Nana?

112
00:05:58,044 --> 00:05:59,091
Yes.

113
00:05:59,850 --> 00:06:00,969
I think it's a great idea.

114
00:06:00,994 --> 00:06:03,223
I was actually going to
suggest it to Uncle too.

115
00:06:03,572 --> 00:06:06,250
We've been using
the same old design forever.

116
00:06:06,599 --> 00:06:09,230
You've got some good ideas, Nana.

117
00:06:09,452 --> 00:06:11,444
Start by giving the front line
a makeover, right?

118
00:06:13,438 --> 00:06:16,753
Exactly, March. Anything that
isn't working needs to change.

119
00:06:17,428 --> 00:06:18,428
Right, Belle?

120
00:06:19,410 --> 00:06:20,424
Right.

121
00:06:24,234 --> 00:06:26,772
And I'm not just changing
the caddie uniforms.

122
00:06:26,797 --> 00:06:30,307
I'm changing the manager too.

123
00:06:40,834 --> 00:06:42,607
Nana, you can't do this.

124
00:06:42,632 --> 00:06:44,632
I've helped Uncle
run this course for years.

125
00:06:44,975 --> 00:06:47,008
Besides, we're family.

126
00:06:48,532 --> 00:06:52,372
Exactly, March. Family shouldn't
steal from family.

127
00:06:53,138 --> 00:06:54,638
What are you talking about?

128
00:06:54,663 --> 00:06:56,573
Who's been feeding you
this nonsense?

129
00:06:56,715 --> 00:06:57,846
Belle?

130
00:06:58,274 --> 00:07:00,314
I don't think this course
is struggling

131
00:07:00,339 --> 00:07:02,738
because we don't have
good enough people running it.

132
00:07:03,269 --> 00:07:05,530
It's struggling because
we hired someone who steals.

133
00:07:08,530 --> 00:07:11,413
- Belle, are you sure?
- I'm not just sure.

134
00:07:11,730 --> 00:07:13,539
The numbers and the paperwork

135
00:07:13,564 --> 00:07:15,420
prove exactly
what he's been doing.

136
00:07:16,610 --> 00:07:18,870
I've known for ages
that he's into online gambling.

137
00:07:18,895 --> 00:07:20,418
Sports betting too.

138
00:07:20,443 --> 00:07:21,736
How do you know?

139
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:23,882
I had him put twenty
on Man United for me.

140
00:07:25,517 --> 00:07:27,333
Think very carefully
about what you do next.

141
00:07:27,358 --> 00:07:29,270
If he's willing
to steal from his own family,

142
00:07:29,295 --> 00:07:31,589
he probably won't hesitate
to do something worse.

143
00:07:32,379 --> 00:07:33,726
I'm not afraid.

144
00:07:34,942 --> 00:07:36,579
If we weren't family,

145
00:07:37,306 --> 00:07:38,924
I would've already gone
to the police.

146
00:07:39,479 --> 00:07:41,456
It's bad enough
that you're terrible at your job.

147
00:07:41,934 --> 00:07:43,053
You're dishonest too.

148
00:07:44,067 --> 00:07:46,621
People who aren't good enough
can improve.

149
00:07:46,646 --> 00:07:48,835
But people who steal
have no place here.

150
00:07:52,466 --> 00:07:55,471
Fine. Just you wait.

151
00:07:56,359 --> 00:08:00,032
I'll shut this course down
and wipe its name off the map.

152
00:08:00,651 --> 00:08:01,722
Just watch me.

153
00:08:22,686 --> 00:08:24,503
A little more roll
would've been nice.

154
00:08:25,718 --> 00:08:27,162
Still can't get the pace right.

155
00:08:41,702 --> 00:08:45,072
I heard you fired
the course manager.

156
00:08:47,361 --> 00:08:48,365
Yes.

157
00:08:48,390 --> 00:08:51,666
I found out he wasn't
exactly treating our course well.

158
00:08:52,467 --> 00:08:53,861
Have you found a replacement?

159
00:08:55,575 --> 00:08:58,223
Not yet.
But I don't think it'll be hard.

160
00:08:58,930 --> 00:09:01,445
Running a golf course isn't easy.

161
00:09:01,470 --> 00:09:03,436
You can't just put
anyone in charge.

162
00:09:05,730 --> 00:09:10,719
I know. But I don't think
firing March was a mistake.

163
00:09:11,610 --> 00:09:16,338
The heart of a golf course
is L-O-V-E.

164
00:09:18,311 --> 00:09:20,660
L is Local First.

165
00:09:20,685 --> 00:09:23,027
Take care of
our own people first.

166
00:09:23,227 --> 00:09:25,726
O is Open Experience.

167
00:09:25,751 --> 00:09:28,441
Offer experiences
that go beyond just playing golf.

168
00:09:28,623 --> 00:09:30,834
There should always be
something new to discover here.

169
00:09:30,859 --> 00:09:33,321
V is Value Over Price.

170
00:09:33,346 --> 00:09:35,760
Create value beyond
simply being good for the price.

171
00:09:35,785 --> 00:09:37,503
Don't compete on price.

172
00:09:37,528 --> 00:09:39,930
E is Emotional Connection.

173
00:09:40,104 --> 00:09:43,481
Create an emotional connection
with everyone who comes here.

174
00:09:45,108 --> 00:09:47,780
Wow. That makes so much sense.

175
00:09:48,272 --> 00:09:51,200
Then I guess
I'm on the right track.

176
00:09:51,745 --> 00:09:54,645
Thanks for saying
you love me, Pro Vee.

177
00:09:54,947 --> 00:09:55,995
What?

178
00:09:56,417 --> 00:10:00,682
L-O-V-E.

179
00:10:03,970 --> 00:10:04,987
Love you too.

180
00:10:27,351 --> 00:10:31,678
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

181
00:10:32,284 --> 00:10:37,606
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

182
00:10:37,631 --> 00:10:42,053
♪ Together, we'll race
toward the line ♪

183
00:10:42,659 --> 00:10:47,067
♪ Chasing the dream
that's yours and mine ♪

184
00:10:47,735 --> 00:10:52,868
♪ In the end,
I know we'll make it there ♪

185
00:10:52,893 --> 00:10:57,992
♪ Just one rule
for you and me to share ♪

186
00:10:58,017 --> 00:11:00,988
♪ Promise you'll stay
close to me ♪

187
00:11:01,013 --> 00:11:03,507
♪ Hold me in your arms
so tenderly ♪

188
00:11:03,532 --> 00:11:09,141
♪ I've never bowed
to anyone in sight ♪

189
00:11:09,174 --> 00:11:12,304
♪ But for you,
I'd surrender without a fight ♪

190
00:11:12,329 --> 00:11:17,157
♪ Just take my hand
and hold it tight ♪

191
00:11:23,860 --> 00:11:26,195
What are you making,
my beautiful Chef Queen?

192
00:11:26,220 --> 00:11:28,339
It smells amazing
all the way from the 19th hole.

193
00:11:28,364 --> 00:11:30,301
The 19th hole?

194
00:11:30,326 --> 00:11:32,216
Let's stick to the 18th.

195
00:11:32,241 --> 00:11:37,099
Because the "19th hole"
means something else entirely.

196
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:42,367
Ohhh... that.

197
00:11:44,179 --> 00:11:45,696
Well, I've got
nothing else to do,

198
00:11:45,721 --> 00:11:52,182
so I thought I'd make
a mixed grill for our big boss.

199
00:11:52,207 --> 00:11:53,559
For me?

200
00:11:53,584 --> 00:11:56,666
Yes. Looks good, doesn't it?

201
00:11:57,380 --> 00:12:02,246
I'm going all out to spite
this sad, lonely, empty kitchen.

202
00:12:02,271 --> 00:12:06,930
I'm so alone in here,
I might as well be on Mars.

203
00:12:06,955 --> 00:12:09,021
With food this good,

204
00:12:09,046 --> 00:12:11,494
this could be a real selling
point for the golf course.

205
00:12:12,857 --> 00:12:15,414
Exactly. Want me to help?

206
00:12:16,062 --> 00:12:20,602
I've got quite a few dishes
I'm really confident in.

207
00:12:20,627 --> 00:12:22,399
There's the mixed grill,

208
00:12:22,423 --> 00:12:26,849
Chuichai Salad, sour mullet soup,
and scrambled eggs with tomatoes.

209
00:12:26,874 --> 00:12:29,360
I stand by all of them.
Want me to put together a plan?

210
00:12:29,385 --> 00:12:32,185
I'm telling you,
they're going to go viral.

211
00:12:32,210 --> 00:12:34,554
Perfect.
Please get on it right away.

212
00:12:34,579 --> 00:12:36,834
Absolutely.
But for now...

213
00:12:36,859 --> 00:12:40,045
accept this humble offering
from the number-one chef

214
00:12:40,070 --> 00:12:44,878
of Goodview Golf Club.

215
00:12:47,898 --> 00:12:49,608
That looks amazing.

216
00:12:51,301 --> 00:12:52,761
Are you gonna eat all that?

217
00:12:53,539 --> 00:12:55,222
Careful.
You'll gain weight, Miss Nana.

218
00:13:01,665 --> 00:13:03,939
- Wanna eat?
- Huh?

219
00:13:04,622 --> 00:13:07,879
Chef Queen made all this,
and I can't finish it by myself.

220
00:13:07,904 --> 00:13:09,284
Come eat with me, Pro Vee.

221
00:13:26,879 --> 00:13:29,768
- Do you eat beef?
- Yeah.

222
00:13:30,588 --> 00:13:32,801
- Chicken?
- I eat pretty much anything.

223
00:13:34,318 --> 00:13:36,283
- What about you?
- Hmm?

224
00:13:36,521 --> 00:13:39,197
I'm not picky at all.
I'll eat anything.

225
00:13:39,890 --> 00:13:41,463
What about shrimp?
Aren't you allergic?

226
00:13:43,359 --> 00:13:44,717
You remembered?

227
00:13:47,716 --> 00:13:49,953
So what's your favorite thing
on this plate?

228
00:13:50,448 --> 00:13:53,107
- Nothing.
- Why not?

229
00:13:53,507 --> 00:13:56,404
My favorite's on that plate.

230
00:14:01,743 --> 00:14:03,009
I didn't know.

231
00:14:06,471 --> 00:14:07,678
Thank you.

232
00:14:08,301 --> 00:14:10,651
You're so sweet, Pro Vee.

233
00:14:11,588 --> 00:14:14,042
If it's something I really like,
I don't usually share.

234
00:14:15,064 --> 00:14:17,584
Unless it's with someone...

235
00:14:34,584 --> 00:14:36,488
Do you have any ketchup?

236
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:39,424
I'll get it for you. One sec.

237
00:14:49,794 --> 00:14:52,833
I've had this forever.
I barely use it.

238
00:15:04,590 --> 00:15:06,784
Hey, hold on.
Let me wipe that off.

239
00:16:07,176 --> 00:16:10,604
What's with your mouth?
It's on your cheek.

240
00:16:13,370 --> 00:16:15,308
I thought there was some
on my lips too.

241
00:16:36,270 --> 00:16:40,294
I'm so full. Too bad I didn't ask
Chef Queen to pack dessert.

242
00:16:40,854 --> 00:16:43,212
I'll check the fridge
and see if there's anything.

243
00:16:43,989 --> 00:16:44,991
Okay.

244
00:16:55,974 --> 00:16:57,983
There's only chocolate.
Want some?

245
00:16:58,252 --> 00:16:59,387
I'll have one.

246
00:17:08,919 --> 00:17:10,822
It's dark chocolate.
A little bitter.

247
00:17:13,120 --> 00:17:14,771
It might taste bitter at first,

248
00:17:14,914 --> 00:17:17,448
but I think there's
a little sweetness underneath.

249
00:17:17,956 --> 00:17:20,932
Kind of like someone I know.
Acts all tough,

250
00:17:21,425 --> 00:17:22,761
but she's secretly sweet.

251
00:17:28,747 --> 00:17:31,225
Did you know that
in ancient times,

252
00:17:31,250 --> 00:17:34,574
chocolate was considered
the food of the gods?

253
00:17:34,950 --> 00:17:36,412
Never heard that before.

254
00:17:39,464 --> 00:17:42,664
It was even used
in sacred rituals.

255
00:17:43,243 --> 00:17:47,234
But these days,
it's become a symbol of love.

256
00:17:47,511 --> 00:17:49,844
When you like someone,

257
00:17:49,869 --> 00:17:51,869
you give them chocolate
to show how you feel.

258
00:17:56,976 --> 00:17:57,992
Oh!

259
00:18:01,701 --> 00:18:05,107
Did you know chocolate
is good for golfers too?

260
00:18:05,858 --> 00:18:06,873
How?

261
00:18:07,547 --> 00:18:10,544
It has flavonoids
that help keep your brain alert,

262
00:18:10,569 --> 00:18:12,951
reduce stress,
and give you energy.

263
00:18:12,976 --> 00:18:14,197
And most importantly...

264
00:18:16,411 --> 00:18:18,085
it's good for your heart.

265
00:18:23,449 --> 00:18:26,634
It helps improve blood flow
and lower blood pressure,

266
00:18:27,142 --> 00:18:29,123
lower bad cholesterol
and raise the good kind.

267
00:18:29,148 --> 00:18:31,457
And most importantly,
it's delicious.

268
00:18:34,571 --> 00:18:36,571
Sounds like one piece
might not be enough.

269
00:18:36,655 --> 00:18:38,218
Want another?
I'll go get you one.

270
00:18:38,590 --> 00:18:42,148
That's enough. I've had enough
sweetness for today.

271
00:18:51,378 --> 00:18:53,874
- Want some, Pro Vee?
- No, you have it.

272
00:18:55,207 --> 00:18:56,659
It's good for golfers.

273
00:18:56,951 --> 00:18:58,236
I'm good. I'm full.

274
00:18:59,792 --> 00:19:01,466
It's good for your heart too.

275
00:19:02,142 --> 00:19:03,590
What a shame.

276
00:19:05,792 --> 00:19:07,109
Just eat it.

277
00:20:25,187 --> 00:20:27,069
Your guest is here, Miss Nana.

278
00:20:29,466 --> 00:20:30,959
Nut!

279
00:20:33,288 --> 00:20:36,791
Wow, it's been forever.
You've gotten even more handsome.

280
00:20:37,029 --> 00:20:40,969
Come on! Flattering me
the second I walk in?

281
00:20:41,643 --> 00:20:44,210
You definitely
want something from me.

282
00:20:44,874 --> 00:20:46,558
You always see right through me.

283
00:20:47,351 --> 00:20:50,521
Belle, sweetie, can I have
a minute alone with Nut?

284
00:20:50,584 --> 00:20:52,998
Of course. Just call me
if you need anything.

285
00:20:54,854 --> 00:20:56,531
- Please have a seat.
- All right.

286
00:21:02,251 --> 00:21:04,327
So, what's this about?

287
00:21:04,771 --> 00:21:07,073
Has Aom told you
anything about me?

288
00:21:07,735 --> 00:21:13,254
Just that you got called back
to run the golf course.

289
00:21:13,718 --> 00:21:18,205
Yeah. I have six months to
make this place profitable again.

290
00:21:18,299 --> 00:21:20,217
So I need someone with experience

291
00:21:20,242 --> 00:21:21,984
and someone I can trust.

292
00:21:22,009 --> 00:21:24,444
Wait. Me?

293
00:21:25,410 --> 00:21:27,831
I've only ever worked
in hotels and resorts.

294
00:21:27,856 --> 00:21:30,134
Golf courses
are a whole different world.

295
00:21:30,468 --> 00:21:33,487
Same world.
Just different shoes.

296
00:21:36,211 --> 00:21:38,294
Okay. Explain.

297
00:21:38,620 --> 00:21:42,215
Hotels sell experiences.
Golf courses do too.

298
00:21:42,583 --> 00:21:45,710
People don't come here just
to hit a ball around and leave.

299
00:21:46,106 --> 00:21:49,104
They come for the atmosphere
and great service.

300
00:21:49,341 --> 00:21:50,968
If we give them
an experience they love,

301
00:21:50,993 --> 00:21:52,626
they'll keep coming back.

302
00:21:53,737 --> 00:21:56,628
Wow. You've gotten
pretty good at this.

303
00:21:58,303 --> 00:22:00,827
Do you play golf?

304
00:22:02,099 --> 00:22:04,108
Yeah. I still play
pretty regularly

305
00:22:04,133 --> 00:22:05,742
with my friends
from school in England.

306
00:22:05,767 --> 00:22:06,777
Perfect.

307
00:22:07,176 --> 00:22:09,763
Aom said you're thinking
about changing jobs.

308
00:22:11,152 --> 00:22:12,844
There's a new resort opening.

309
00:22:12,869 --> 00:22:14,960
They made me a pretty good offer.

310
00:22:14,985 --> 00:22:16,770
I'll beat their offer.

311
00:22:17,478 --> 00:22:20,633
Oh! Big-spender CEO.

312
00:22:21,093 --> 00:22:24,872
You've managed teams and
handled problems on the ground.

313
00:22:24,930 --> 00:22:26,971
You've brought quiet places
back to life.

314
00:22:27,393 --> 00:22:29,594
That's exactly
what this place needs.

315
00:22:31,269 --> 00:22:32,805
So who was running it before?

316
00:22:33,813 --> 00:22:35,276
- I fired him.
- Why?

317
00:22:35,301 --> 00:22:37,832
- Fraud.
- Oh.

318
00:22:40,336 --> 00:22:45,689
But I've never managed
a golf course before.

319
00:22:46,304 --> 00:22:47,565
I just know how to play.

320
00:22:48,014 --> 00:22:49,694
But you know people.

321
00:22:50,180 --> 00:22:52,474
And people are the biggest
investment in any business.

322
00:22:52,994 --> 00:22:55,573
I need someone who knows

323
00:22:55,598 --> 00:22:57,049
how to manage people,
not just turf.

324
00:22:58,689 --> 00:23:02,745
Did you go to fashion school
or business school?

325
00:23:04,952 --> 00:23:07,713
Come on, Nut.
Please help me.

326
00:23:08,078 --> 00:23:10,078
Please?

327
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:13,997
Pretty please?

328
00:23:22,748 --> 00:23:25,065
Why the sudden decision to leave?

329
00:23:25,090 --> 00:23:27,311
You've worked for
Sanchai for years.

330
00:23:28,303 --> 00:23:30,453
He was too busy
with his other businesses

331
00:23:30,478 --> 00:23:31,993
to pay attention to the course.

332
00:23:32,685 --> 00:23:34,641
But the moment things went wrong,
he blamed me.

333
00:23:35,251 --> 00:23:38,959
I heard he's put his daughter
in charge now.

334
00:23:39,342 --> 00:23:43,324
The daughter who studied fashion
and knows nothing about golf.

335
00:23:44,126 --> 00:23:45,483
How long can that possibly last?

336
00:23:46,049 --> 00:23:48,899
So you're jumping ship
before it sinks.

337
00:23:51,869 --> 00:23:56,406
I know you want to see
that place go under too.

338
00:24:00,332 --> 00:24:01,588
I can help you.

339
00:24:03,072 --> 00:24:04,859
I know everything
about that place.

340
00:24:53,487 --> 00:24:57,438
Hello, Pro Jin. I'm here.
Where should I meet you?

341
00:25:15,194 --> 00:25:17,627
Hi, Pro Jin.

342
00:25:17,857 --> 00:25:19,314
Hi, Miss Nana.

343
00:25:21,366 --> 00:25:24,826
Sorry.
I'm almost 20 minutes late.

344
00:25:24,945 --> 00:25:26,758
No worries. Take it easy.

345
00:25:28,203 --> 00:25:30,720
I'm ready.
Shall we get started?

346
00:26:17,341 --> 00:26:20,251
- Not bad for your first time.
- Thank you.

347
00:26:21,520 --> 00:26:23,735
Have you taken lessons before?

348
00:26:24,817 --> 00:26:28,154
I am, actually. I'm taking
lessons from Pro Vee at Goodview.

349
00:26:29,172 --> 00:26:31,563
Oh. Pro Vee.

350
00:26:33,908 --> 00:26:35,908
I always thought we were friends.

351
00:26:39,033 --> 00:26:41,017
But the way you beat me today...

352
00:26:42,964 --> 00:26:44,361
was dirty.

353
00:27:05,563 --> 00:27:07,369
You know Pro Vee?

354
00:27:08,900 --> 00:27:09,976
Very well.

355
00:27:12,918 --> 00:27:16,298
I think I'll call it a day.
We can do this again sometime.

356
00:27:22,795 --> 00:27:23,950
Are you okay?

357
00:27:25,133 --> 00:27:26,180
You sure you're okay?

358
00:27:28,351 --> 00:27:31,776
I'm fine.
I think I just stood up too fast.

359
00:27:32,021 --> 00:27:34,299
You sure you're okay?
Want something sweet to drink?

360
00:27:34,614 --> 00:27:36,488
I'm fine. Really.

361
00:27:37,417 --> 00:27:39,107
If anything happens to you here,

362
00:27:39,132 --> 00:27:41,132
the people at Goodview
might not be happy.

363
00:27:43,522 --> 00:27:45,845
I'll get going. Bye.

364
00:27:57,443 --> 00:27:59,465
Pro Vee! Oh, Pro Vee!

365
00:27:59,490 --> 00:28:01,141
Are you heading back
to the staff housing?

366
00:28:01,165 --> 00:28:03,418
- Yes.
- Wait, wait! Hold on!

367
00:28:07,600 --> 00:28:11,048
Oh! Why are you heading back
so early today?

368
00:28:11,073 --> 00:28:14,184
- I don't have any lessons today.
- Oh, that's good!

369
00:28:14,595 --> 00:28:17,229
Not really.
Having lessons would be better.

370
00:28:17,254 --> 00:28:19,570
Did you need something,
Chef Queen?

371
00:28:20,655 --> 00:28:23,179
Here. I brought you some dessert.

372
00:28:23,330 --> 00:28:26,705
It's Bua Loi with sweet egg.

373
00:28:26,730 --> 00:28:29,455
- This one's for you.
- Thank you.

374
00:28:29,480 --> 00:28:32,495
And could you give this one
to Miss Nana for me?

375
00:28:32,770 --> 00:28:33,801
Sure.

376
00:28:34,690 --> 00:28:36,619
And tell her to eat it.

377
00:28:36,644 --> 00:28:38,525
It might cure
all that daydreaming

378
00:28:38,549 --> 00:28:43,521
and pining over someone.

379
00:28:43,951 --> 00:28:47,146
She's been spacing out all day.
Like this.

380
00:28:49,331 --> 00:28:50,665
Completely gone.

381
00:28:50,690 --> 00:28:54,614
I looked over this afternoon
and she was just like this.

382
00:28:54,639 --> 00:28:56,289
No idea who she was
thinking about.

383
00:28:59,286 --> 00:29:00,350
Yeah...

384
00:29:03,307 --> 00:29:06,773
Like this all day.
Just staring off into space...

385
00:29:17,235 --> 00:29:18,289
Nana?

386
00:29:20,813 --> 00:29:21,854
Nana?

387
00:29:23,961 --> 00:29:25,011
Nana?

388
00:29:26,003 --> 00:29:27,026
Nana?

389
00:29:28,673 --> 00:29:29,681
Nana?

390
00:29:32,775 --> 00:29:33,775
Nana?

391
00:29:38,122 --> 00:29:40,049
Nana, are you okay?

392
00:29:43,090 --> 00:29:44,943
Why are you burning up?

393
00:30:22,977 --> 00:30:27,606
I have to do this.
Just watch me, Pro Vee.

394
00:30:28,592 --> 00:30:30,785
Hole seven. Par five.

395
00:30:33,031 --> 00:30:35,860
Double bogey.
Choo-choo...

396
00:31:07,473 --> 00:31:09,819
Pro Vee... don't leave me.

397
00:31:11,122 --> 00:31:12,973
I'll do it.

398
00:31:18,338 --> 00:31:19,679
I'm right here.

399
00:32:46,801 --> 00:32:48,742
ProVee? What are you doing here?

400
00:32:50,960 --> 00:32:52,960
Your fever got really high
last night.

401
00:32:53,130 --> 00:32:57,662
So I stayed to cool you down,
and I must've fallen asleep.

402
00:33:04,230 --> 00:33:06,611
I didn't change your clothes
or do anything else,

403
00:33:06,636 --> 00:33:07,897
so don't worry.

404
00:33:08,525 --> 00:33:11,400
Aw, too bad.
You could've changed me.

405
00:33:11,542 --> 00:33:13,490
- What?
- Kidding.

406
00:33:14,223 --> 00:33:16,987
Thank you for staying with me
all night.

407
00:33:18,090 --> 00:33:20,457
Your fever's down now,
so I'll get going.

408
00:33:20,822 --> 00:33:22,230
See you at the course.

409
00:33:24,199 --> 00:33:27,832
It's my day off.
You should get some rest too.

410
00:33:28,043 --> 00:33:29,558
It's good to be determined,

411
00:33:29,583 --> 00:33:31,583
but you need to
take care of yourself too.

412
00:33:32,985 --> 00:33:35,648
What do you do on your days off?

413
00:33:36,250 --> 00:33:37,323
Why do you ask?

414
00:33:41,331 --> 00:33:44,181
I'm curious what golf pros do

415
00:33:44,206 --> 00:33:47,038
on their days off.

416
00:33:50,499 --> 00:33:53,038
Can I tag along with you
for a day?

417
00:33:57,297 --> 00:33:58,353
What?

418
00:34:24,931 --> 00:34:28,186
Why is Pro Vee coming out
of Miss Nana's room this early?

419
00:34:31,531 --> 00:34:35,368
Wait... are those two...?

420
00:34:52,820 --> 00:34:55,924
- Who did you bring home, Vee?
- It's Nana.

421
00:35:02,883 --> 00:35:04,540
Uncle Sanchai's daughter.

422
00:35:08,036 --> 00:35:09,401
Oh!

423
00:35:10,459 --> 00:35:14,374
Nana, look at you.
You're all grown up now.

424
00:35:14,937 --> 00:35:17,552
- Hello, Auntie.
- Hello, dear.

425
00:35:18,792 --> 00:35:20,453
You probably don't remember me.

426
00:35:21,912 --> 00:35:25,259
Sorry, I don't.

427
00:35:26,762 --> 00:35:28,550
I'm an old friend of your dad's.

428
00:35:28,693 --> 00:35:30,257
I've known you
since you were little,

429
00:35:30,384 --> 00:35:33,018
back when you used to run around
the golf course with Vee.

430
00:35:33,863 --> 00:35:35,689
Oh!

431
00:35:35,714 --> 00:35:38,542
Vee, you should've told me
you were bringing Nana over.

432
00:35:38,567 --> 00:35:40,044
I would've prepared something.

433
00:35:40,069 --> 00:35:41,695
Oh, no, it's fine.

434
00:35:41,720 --> 00:35:43,969
It's Pro Vee's day off today,

435
00:35:43,994 --> 00:35:45,263
and I happened to be free,

436
00:35:45,288 --> 00:35:47,089
so I asked if I could tag along
for the day.

437
00:35:48,510 --> 00:35:50,579
Of course.
Make yourself at home.

438
00:35:50,604 --> 00:35:54,304
I'm heading out to buy some
paint and a few other things.

439
00:35:54,329 --> 00:35:57,370
- Stay for dinner, okay?
- I'd love to.

440
00:35:57,575 --> 00:36:00,724
I was hoping
you'd feed me anyway.

441
00:36:01,791 --> 00:36:05,164
Of course.
I'll be back soon, sweetheart.

442
00:36:05,579 --> 00:36:06,595
Okay.

443
00:36:12,276 --> 00:36:15,001
Wow, these are beautiful.

444
00:36:15,026 --> 00:36:17,026
Did your mom paint all of these?

445
00:36:17,695 --> 00:36:18,742
Mm-hmm.

446
00:36:23,248 --> 00:36:25,393
This one looks like our course.

447
00:36:27,127 --> 00:36:28,212
I think it is.

448
00:36:28,466 --> 00:36:30,082
Do you paint too?

449
00:36:30,733 --> 00:36:32,955
Mom taught me watercolor
when I was little.

450
00:36:33,062 --> 00:36:36,689
It teaches you focus,
a calm mind, and a steady hand.

451
00:36:36,752 --> 00:36:39,550
And how to hold on to a moment.

452
00:36:39,701 --> 00:36:43,999
Wow. You somehow managed
to turn watercolor into golf.

453
00:36:44,359 --> 00:36:47,598
Watercolor is all about timing.

454
00:36:47,915 --> 00:36:49,903
Knowing when to apply pressure,

455
00:36:50,130 --> 00:36:53,731
and sometimes having the courage
to just let it flow.

456
00:36:54,670 --> 00:36:55,710
Just like golf.

457
00:36:56,987 --> 00:36:58,899
Too tense,
and you won't hit well.

458
00:36:58,924 --> 00:37:01,201
Too relaxed,
and you won't either.

459
00:37:01,353 --> 00:37:04,054
It's about rhythm,
your breathing,

460
00:37:04,173 --> 00:37:07,216
and most importantly,
accepting that

461
00:37:07,241 --> 00:37:09,288
once the club makes contact
with the ball,

462
00:37:09,313 --> 00:37:10,889
it's out of your hands.

463
00:37:11,412 --> 00:37:13,760
Ooh... That's deep.

464
00:37:14,303 --> 00:37:16,851
Can I try painting something too?

465
00:37:20,539 --> 00:37:21,746
Too easy.

466
00:37:26,670 --> 00:37:29,881
Put the clay down
and press it onto the wheel.

467
00:37:33,951 --> 00:37:37,215
Okay. Now wet your hands

468
00:37:37,240 --> 00:37:38,842
and place them on the clay.

469
00:37:41,614 --> 00:37:44,683
- Whoa, too much!
- Oh!

470
00:37:45,976 --> 00:37:48,822
Press the pedal gently and
the wheel will start spinning.

471
00:37:51,104 --> 00:37:53,365
Whoa, too hard.

472
00:37:53,390 --> 00:37:56,194
Easy. Just a light touch.

473
00:37:58,935 --> 00:38:01,611
Slowly. Slowly.

474
00:38:04,504 --> 00:38:08,292
Okay. Now use your hands
to shape the clay upward.

475
00:38:08,756 --> 00:38:10,423
Keep your hands steady.

476
00:38:12,354 --> 00:38:15,631
If you press too hard, it'll
wobble out of shape like that.

477
00:38:15,994 --> 00:38:19,056
Keep your touch light
and apply pressure gradually.

478
00:38:19,701 --> 00:38:20,935
Focus.

479
00:38:21,483 --> 00:38:23,791
Pay attention
to every little movement.

480
00:38:27,606 --> 00:38:29,218
Come here.
I'll help you.

481
00:39:04,733 --> 00:39:05,836
Pro Vee...

482
00:39:45,366 --> 00:39:48,770
- Hey, stop. Focus!
- Oh!

483
00:39:49,344 --> 00:39:50,781
Sorry.

484
00:39:55,245 --> 00:39:58,591
See what happens when you
lose focus for even a second?

485
00:39:59,649 --> 00:40:00,791
Let's do it again.

486
00:40:01,264 --> 00:40:03,271
Okay... how?

487
00:40:05,250 --> 00:40:07,250
Slowly. Keep it spinning gently.

488
00:40:09,714 --> 00:40:11,152
Slowly, slowly.

489
00:40:22,514 --> 00:40:24,188
Careful. Not too fast.

490
00:40:35,861 --> 00:40:39,074
Let it set first,
then it can go in the kiln.

491
00:40:39,099 --> 00:40:42,605
Leave it there. We'll fire it
with Mom's other pieces.

492
00:40:42,630 --> 00:40:44,361
So that means
I have to come back, right?

493
00:40:44,889 --> 00:40:48,166
And after it's fired,
we still have to paint it. Right?

494
00:40:52,411 --> 00:40:53,810
Want to go wash your hands?

495
00:40:55,913 --> 00:40:58,143
Yeah. I'm covered in clay.

496
00:41:13,046 --> 00:41:15,870
- Hungry?
- Starving.

497
00:41:15,895 --> 00:41:17,021
What do you want to eat?

498
00:41:18,019 --> 00:41:19,996
Shouldn't we wait for your mom?

499
00:41:20,210 --> 00:41:24,164
She texted me. She ran into
a friend, so she'll be a while.

500
00:41:24,297 --> 00:41:26,594
You can sit and wait here.

501
00:41:28,018 --> 00:41:32,070
What are you making?
I'll help.

502
00:41:37,047 --> 00:41:39,278
- Here.
- Thanks.

503
00:41:41,987 --> 00:41:43,083
Mmm. That's good.

504
00:41:43,150 --> 00:41:46,182
Hey, don't eat it yet. Wait.

505
00:41:48,336 --> 00:41:50,415
- What now?
- Such vibrant colors!

506
00:41:51,896 --> 00:41:53,102
Do it properly.

507
00:41:54,748 --> 00:41:56,517
Ow, Pro Vee!

508
00:42:05,767 --> 00:42:08,339
And then... like this.

509
00:42:13,418 --> 00:42:14,426
What?

510
00:42:16,024 --> 00:42:19,096
Ow, my eyes!

511
00:42:20,314 --> 00:42:22,084
It really stings.

512
00:42:24,612 --> 00:42:25,969
Don't cry.

513
00:42:30,299 --> 00:42:31,333
The peel will...

514
00:42:38,683 --> 00:42:41,056
Come on, hurry up.
When are you going to boil?

515
00:42:43,746 --> 00:42:45,244
Good job, Pro Vee.

516
00:43:06,903 --> 00:43:09,117
What? Is it bad?

517
00:43:11,155 --> 00:43:12,155
It's hot.

518
00:43:22,595 --> 00:43:26,469
That looks so good.
Can I dig in now?

519
00:43:26,661 --> 00:43:28,018
Sure.

520
00:43:34,714 --> 00:43:36,133
Thank you.

521
00:43:36,870 --> 00:43:37,871
Please.

522
00:43:39,770 --> 00:43:40,849
Want some omelet too?

523
00:43:44,796 --> 00:43:47,310
Mmm. This is really good.

524
00:43:48,573 --> 00:43:49,914
Thanks.

525
00:43:51,415 --> 00:43:54,927
- Which one do you like best?
- I like...

526
00:43:56,512 --> 00:43:57,528
This one.

527
00:43:57,742 --> 00:43:59,433
- The omelet?
- Yeah.

528
00:43:59,458 --> 00:44:00,911
That's the easiest thing.

529
00:44:03,714 --> 00:44:06,543
- The food's really good.
- Want a bite?

530
00:44:07,648 --> 00:44:08,712
Mm-hmm.

531
00:44:15,724 --> 00:44:18,230
Mmm. It really is good.

532
00:44:18,413 --> 00:44:19,487
Good, right?

533
00:44:24,231 --> 00:44:27,105
Whoever chopped these onions
must be really talented.

534
00:44:27,130 --> 00:44:29,338
- They're absolutely delicious.
- I'm offended.

535
00:44:32,746 --> 00:44:33,781
Now I'm sulking.

536
00:44:40,827 --> 00:44:44,614
Sorry I wasn't here. You had to
settle for Vee's cooking today.

537
00:44:45,391 --> 00:44:47,216
Pro Vee's actually
a pretty good cook.

538
00:44:47,241 --> 00:44:49,264
I ate till I was stuffed.

539
00:44:49,785 --> 00:44:51,986
Next time, come try my cooking.

540
00:44:52,654 --> 00:44:57,350
I'll leave my one-of-a-kind
masterpiece with you.

541
00:44:57,551 --> 00:45:00,298
Of course. I'll keep it
safe after it's fired

542
00:45:00,323 --> 00:45:01,957
until you come back to paint it.

543
00:45:02,182 --> 00:45:04,983
I had so much fun today.
Thank you.

544
00:45:05,062 --> 00:45:07,350
Next time, you can try
watercolor painting too.

545
00:45:07,375 --> 00:45:08,819
To work on my concentration,
right?

546
00:45:08,844 --> 00:45:09,882
Mm-hmm.

547
00:45:12,524 --> 00:45:14,054
I'm heading out, Mom.

548
00:45:14,079 --> 00:45:17,367
All right. Come visit again
when you're both free.

549
00:45:17,392 --> 00:45:18,399
We will.

550
00:45:18,555 --> 00:45:19,599
- Goodbye.
- Bye, dear.

551
00:45:19,624 --> 00:45:21,202
- Goodbye.
- Get home safe.

552
00:45:21,227 --> 00:45:22,647
Thank you. Goodbye.

553
00:45:29,160 --> 00:45:30,528
Mom?

554
00:45:32,353 --> 00:45:36,732
Can Nana come live with us?

555
00:45:38,298 --> 00:45:40,612
She has her own home, sweetheart.

556
00:45:41,001 --> 00:45:45,099
But I like Nana.
I want her to live with us

557
00:45:45,124 --> 00:45:46,870
so we won't be lonely.

558
00:45:46,895 --> 00:45:48,505
Whenever we have some free time,

559
00:45:48,869 --> 00:45:51,398
we can always go play with her.

560
00:45:51,636 --> 00:45:55,011
But I want to be with
Nana all the time.

561
00:45:55,036 --> 00:45:59,578
When I grow up,
can I marry Nana?

562
00:46:19,618 --> 00:46:23,401
Thank you for today, Pro Vee.
I had so much fun.

563
00:46:23,956 --> 00:46:26,239
You only have two days left.

564
00:46:26,264 --> 00:46:28,650
I promise I'll give it
everything I've got.

565
00:46:28,675 --> 00:46:31,581
Giving it your all isn't enough.
You have to make it.

566
00:46:31,606 --> 00:46:32,687
Hole seven...

567
00:46:32,711 --> 00:46:35,378
Par five. Two over par.

568
00:46:36,474 --> 00:46:37,545
Choo-choo.

569
00:46:43,737 --> 00:46:46,286
Go get some rest.
You've had a long day.

570
00:46:46,311 --> 00:46:49,921
Okay.
Then good night in advance.

571
00:47:16,333 --> 00:47:19,050
♪ The way you act,
I know you're into me ♪

572
00:47:19,075 --> 00:47:21,981
♪ That racing heart
gives you away so easily ♪

573
00:47:22,006 --> 00:47:25,793
♪ But I'll play clueless,
just wait and see ♪

574
00:47:25,818 --> 00:47:27,818
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

575
00:47:27,843 --> 00:47:30,688
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

576
00:47:30,713 --> 00:47:34,152
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

577
00:47:34,177 --> 00:47:38,878
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

578
00:47:38,903 --> 00:47:40,903
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

579
00:47:45,208 --> 00:47:48,016
Chef Queen prepared
a big dinner spread for us,

580
00:47:48,041 --> 00:47:49,360
so dress up nicely.

581
00:47:49,710 --> 00:47:52,420
Do I really have to
dress up this much?

582
00:47:52,445 --> 00:47:53,460
Do I look good?

583
00:47:53,485 --> 00:47:55,184
Can you start tomorrow?

584
00:47:55,209 --> 00:47:56,423
And about the salary...

585
00:47:56,448 --> 00:47:58,345
I know you probably have
a number in mind.

586
00:47:58,370 --> 00:48:01,728
We can discuss compensation
when you sign tomorrow.

587
00:48:04,397 --> 00:48:07,083
Great.
Who have you been learning from?

588
00:48:07,108 --> 00:48:09,108
Pro Jin at The Royal Green.

589
00:48:09,570 --> 00:48:11,001
They don't get along.

590
00:48:11,026 --> 00:48:12,350
Who doesn't?

591
00:48:12,429 --> 00:48:14,850
Pro Vee and Pro Jin.

592
00:48:17,315 --> 00:48:21,537
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

593
00:48:22,319 --> 00:48:27,393
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

594
00:48:27,418 --> 00:48:31,993
♪ Together, we'll race
toward the line ♪

595
00:48:32,631 --> 00:48:37,054
♪ Chasing the dream
that's yours and mine ♪

596
00:48:37,643 --> 00:48:42,807
♪ In the end,
I know we'll make it there ♪

597
00:48:42,832 --> 00:48:47,032
♪ Just one rule
for you and me to share ♪

598
00:48:47,757 --> 00:48:50,864
♪ Promise you'll stay
close to me ♪

599
00:48:50,889 --> 00:48:53,406
♪ Hold me in your arms
so tenderly ♪

600
00:48:53,431 --> 00:48:59,072
♪ I've never bowed
to anyone in sight ♪

601
00:48:59,097 --> 00:49:02,225
♪ But for you,
I'd surrender without a fight ♪

602
00:49:02,250 --> 00:49:07,093
♪ Just take my hand
and hold it tight ♪

603
00:49:08,272 --> 00:49:11,472
♪ And walk with me
along the way ♪

604
00:49:11,497 --> 00:49:14,110
♪ No matter what it takes
to win someday ♪

605
00:49:14,135 --> 00:49:19,727
♪ Sometimes this tender heart
may despair ♪

606
00:49:19,752 --> 00:49:22,953
♪ But tell me,
why should we care? ♪

607
00:49:22,978 --> 00:49:25,376
♪ When all we need
is love that's fair ♪

608
00:49:25,401 --> 00:49:29,077
♪ In a love we share,
no one has to win or lose ♪

609
00:49:31,241 --> 00:49:35,878
♪ Let my heart answer anew ♪

610
00:49:36,429 --> 00:49:40,970
♪ A thousand rounds,
it'd still choose you ♪

611
00:49:41,385 --> 00:49:46,285
♪ One look in your eyes
is all I need ♪

612
00:49:46,310 --> 00:49:49,769
♪ Oh, baby. I trust your sweet. ♪
